          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: Testimony in 2014 of an old observation. On November 29, 2012, at 6:40 PM, a witness observed from a distance, in the east-southeast direction, the particular and rapid movements (ascending, descending, with direction change, with division) of a bright, red and white light at low altitude in the cloudy sky. No other testimony was collected. This testimony has limited information, as the questionnaire is only partially completed (e.g., duration and speed not reported, only one position of PAN mentioned while movement is described), and the photos mentioned have never been provided despite follow-up with GEIPAN. The testimony concerns an observation made two years earlier. Due to the lack of information, it is not possible to respond to this testimony. Consequently, GEIPAN classifies this case as C: lack of information.",
